HTSAdapter::mintToken(token, amount, metadata) — branching-tree (BTT)
See the Testing section of the Solidity standards (branching-tree technique). Each leaf maps to a
named test in HTSAdapterTest.t.sol; a "given" is a state-setup modifier, a "when" is a parameter
branch, an "it should" is the asserted outcome. Source: HTSAdapterLib.mintToken().

mintToken(token, amount, metadata)
├── given the caller does not hold HTS_OPERATOR_ROLE
│   └── it should revert AccessControlUnauthorizedAccount        → test_MintToken_RevertsForManagerWithoutOperatorRole
└── given the caller holds HTS_OPERATOR_ROLE
    ├── when amount is negative
    │   └── it should revert HTSInvalidAmount                    → test_MintToken_RevertsOnNegativeAmount
    └── when amount is zero or positive
        ├── given the address is not an HTS token (HTS 167)
        │   └── it should revert HTSNotAToken                    → test_MintToken_RevertsWhenNotAToken
        ├── given the token has no supply key (HTS 180)
        │   └── it should revert HTSTokenNoSupplyKey             → test_MintToken_RevertsWithoutSupplyKey
        ├── given the supply key is not the diamond (HTS 326)
        │   └── it should revert HTSKeyNotActive                 → test_MintToken_RevertsWhenSupplyKeyIsNotTheDiamond
        ├── given the mint exceeds the max supply (HTS 236)
        │   └── it should revert HTSMaxSupplyReached             → test_MintToken_RevertsWhenMaxSupplyReached
        └── given the diamond holds the supply key
            ├── when the token is fungible
            │   └── it should mint amount to the treasury        → test_MintToken_MintsFungibleSupplyToTreasury
            └── when the token is non-fungible
                └── it should mint one serial per metadata entry → test_MintToken_MintsNonFungibleSerialsFromMetadata
